);\n  });\n  it(\"should let a live cell with exactly 3 neighbors survive\", () => {\n    const result = nextGeneration([[0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1], [2, 1], [10, 10]]);\n    expect(result).toContainEqual([1, 1]);\n  });\n  it(\"should kill a live cell with 4 neighbors by overpopulation\", () => {\n    const result = nextGeneration([[1, 1], [0, 0], [0, 2], [2, 0], [2, 2]]);\n    expect(result).not.toContainEqual([1, 1]);\n  });\n  it(\"should revive a dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors\", () => {\n    const result = nextGeneration([[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1]]);\n    expect(result).toContainEqual([1, 1]);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should advance a blinker from vertical to horizontal -- [(-1,1), (0,1), (1,1)]\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784969299287},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need refactor. Current implementation duplicates neighbor iteration in countLiveNeighbors and birth loops. Naming could improve. Need run tests first. Also count APP mass before. Need apply simple design rules priority. Naming evaluation: functions: cellKey okay, countLiveNeighbors okay. nextGeneration okay. Some variables: births, checkedBirthCells. Birth logic duplicates neighbor loops. We can extract neighbor coordinate generation? But don't over-engineer. Need at least one refactoring. Possible refactorings:\n- Remove duplicate nested loops by generating all neighbor offsets once and reusing. This can reduce duplication and mass.\n- Rename `NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS` to `NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS` fine. Could define `NEIGHBOR_COORDINATES` as array of [dx,dy] excluding center. Then countLiveNeighbors and birth loops can iterate that. This reduces loops and conditionals. However mass: current countLiveNeighbors has 2 loops (nested), 1 conditional skip, 1 conditional has, 1 assignment count++. Birth has 3 loops (over live cells + nested offsets) plus conditionals. Extracting neighbor coordinates to constant array of 8 elements removes nested loops in countLiveNeighbors (1 lo